  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 778b480bb38e4ef491b41adb778f4536, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LWS.TruckCamping.CampHelpPages
  text: {fileID: 972148218}
  number: {fileID: 1314061732}
  previous: {fileID: 595828377}
  next: {fileID: 729515518}
  pages:
  - 'A WILDERNESS TO SHARE


    No race timer, score or winner. Drive the mountain
    trails to discover lakes, caves, cabins and overlooks. Stop, tap ACTION, then
    use left/right to browse nearby activities and ACTION to choose.


    Gather
    visible sticks, firewood and forage. A campfire needs3sticks and2firewood. Fresh
    fish or forage cooks into2warm meals. At the lake, cast and tap ACTION when the
    bobber dips; missing a bite has no penalty.


    Drive gently up a hammock approach
    until the actual wheels settle on its spring-supported deck, then choose NAP.
    Cabins and rest clearings also allow naps. WAKE returns to exploring.


    PHOTO
    opens a shared scenic camera. The selected owner''s controls orbit, ACTION captures
    a real PNG, and RETURN TO WALK ends the photo. Pause/help freeze the session.
    Save or restore a paused expedition through the existing workshop adapter.'
  - Survival-lite is optional, forgiving hunger/food. No starvation, collision harvesting
    or compulsory leaderboard. Companions actually drive, gather, cook, fish and
    relax.
